[FINAL-TEXT] I have now exhaustively verified every component in the reported fault path. Here is the complete picture:

- **PC4** (172.16.10.4/24, gw 172.16.10.1) → switch1 eth1 → **br_vlan10** ✓
- **Laptop0** (172.16.20.10/24, gw 172.16.20.1) → switch1 eth7 → **br_vlan20** ✓
- **switch1** trunk eth0 carries both eth0.10 (VID 10) and eth0.20 (VID 20) into mswitch1 ✓
- **mswitch1** bridges tagged VLANs across trunk ports (eth0/eth2/eth4) correctly ✓
- **router0** sub-interfaces: eth0.10 VID 10 = 172.16.10.1/24, eth0.20 VID 20 = 172.16.20.1/24, both UP ✓
